# PP435: `go build` in either directory writes its output next to the source, and both outputs were
# tracked for a while - 14.4 MB of unstripped Linux x86-64 that cannot run on the platform this port
# ships to. The source is what documents the PSN token flow; a build of it is not.
#
# Named rather than globbed: a Go binary takes its module's name, so there is no extension to match
# and `*` would swallow the .go files this directory exists for.
holepunch
refresh-token

# And the same on a machine that builds them for Windows.
holepunch.exe
refresh-token.exe
